       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. You've confirmed it, and I'm not questioning your authority as the attending. But 50 mg of amlodipine is a dose that can cause serious harm, and I don't know of any indication that calls for it. It is five times the 10 mg maximum. Amlodipine also has a long half-life of about 30 to 50 hours, so one dose like this could cause profound hypotension and shock that lasts for days. You also haven't given a clinical rationale, and I can't verify one.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter 5 mg or 10 mg once daily** right away. If you need more blood pressure control, I can also enter a second agent from a different class.\n- **Enter the order with a note**, if you give me a specific clinical rationale. I'd still want to flag it for pharmacist review.\n- **Route it through pharmacy or your institution's override process**, if you believe 50 mg is truly warranted. That way a second clinician checks it before administration.\n\nTell me which you'd like."
